# SEI Site Auditor

Internal tool for auditing AEM DAM assets and testimonials across capella.edu. Read PRD.md before implementing any feature.

## Project

React + TypeScript frontend (Vite), Node.js + Express backend, BullMQ + Redis job queue, PostgreSQL via Prisma, perceptual hashing for duplicate detection, Playwright scraper (headless Chromium — required for JS-rendered pages).

## Commands

- `npm run dev` — frontend (5173) + backend (3001) + worker concurrently
- `npm run dev:worker` — BullMQ worker only
- `npm run test` — Jest
- `npm run lint` — ESLint + TypeScript
- `npm run db:migrate` — Prisma migrations

## Architecture

```
UI → API (Express) → Services → Prisma → PostgreSQL
                  ↘ BullMQ Queue → Redis
                          ↓
                     Worker Process
                          ↓
                     Scraper → Prisma → PostgreSQL
```

Route handlers thin — validate, enqueue or call service, respond.
All Prisma queries in `packages/db/repositories/` only.
Worker (`apps/worker/`) separate process — imports queue, scraper, db packages only.
Queue definitions in `packages/queue/` — shared between API and worker.

## Job Queue — Critical

NEVER process more than one page synchronously in an API request.

Audit flow:
1. `POST /api/v1/audit` → create AuditJob + AuditJobUrl rows → enqueue → return `{ jobId }`
2. Worker: batches of 10 URLs → scrape → write results → update `completed_urls`
3. `GET /api/v1/audit/:jobId/status` → UI polls every 3s
4. `GET /api/v1/audit/:jobId/results` → paginated, queryable before job completes
5. One bad URL must never stop the job — mark failed, continue

Input types: paste URLs, CSV/TXT upload, sitemap URL (parse XML `<loc>` elements).

## AEM Context

- Live site: `https://www.capella.edu`
- Asset path: `/content/dam/capella/`
- Page path: `/content/capella/en/`
- Public URLs: `AEM_PUBLIC_HOST` + `aem_path` — never hardcode domain
- Phase 2 needs IT service account (see `.env.example`)

## AEM Query Builder (Phase 2) — Critical Rules

Endpoint: `GET /bin/querybuilder.json` on AEM author host.

**DEFAULT LIMIT IS 10 HITS — always set `p.limit` explicitly or results are silently truncated.**

Key params:
- `p.limit` — always set. Use `-1` for all (caution on large sets)
- `p.hits=selective` + `p.properties` — always prefer over `p.hits=full` to reduce payload
- `p.guessTotal=true` — fast pagination, avoids full count. Returns `more: true` when results exceed limit
- `p.guessTotal=N` — exact count up to N, then `more: true` — best for UI pagination
- `orderby=@jcr:content/cq:lastModified` + `orderby.sort=desc` — recency sort
- `group.p.or=true` — OR logic for grouped predicates (default is AND)
- `1_property`, `2_property` — numeric prefix when using same predicate multiple times
- `tagid` + `tagid.property=jcr:content/cq:tags` — tag matching
- `p.offset` — pagination offset

Performance: always use `p.guessTotal` for large result sets — exact counts require reading entire set for access control, significant perf hit at scale.

Example — find pages referencing an asset:
```
GET /bin/querybuilder.json
  ?path=/content/capella/en
  &type=nt:base
  &property=fileReference
  &property.value=/content/dam/capella/images/hero.jpg
  &p.limit=500
  &p.hits=selective
  &p.properties=path jcr:content/jcr:title jcr:content/cq:lastReplicated
  &p.guessTotal=true
```

## Testimonial Extraction

Two storage types — handle both:
- `structured_component`: `[data-component="testimonial"]`, `.cmp-testimonial`
- `hardcoded_text`: `blockquote`, `[class*="quote"]` + attribution patterns

Selectors (priority order):
1. `[data-component="testimonial"]`
2. `.cmp-testimonial`
3. `.testimonial`, `.student-quote`
4. `blockquote + [class*="name"]`
5. `[class*="quote"] + [class*="student"]`

Deduplication: normalize `quote_text` (lowercase, strip punctuation) as fingerprint.
Upsert on fingerprint. Conflict on `student_name`/`program` → `needs_review = true`, never overwrite.

## Key Routes

```
/audit            → Start audit (paste / upload CSV / sitemap)
/audit/:jobId     → Live progress + streaming results
/lookup           → Asset reverse lookup
/assets           → Browse assets
/assets/:id       → Asset detail
/duplicates       → Duplicate groups
/testimonials     → Search testimonials
/testimonials/:id → Testimonial detail
/programs/coverage → Program coverage gaps (Phase 2)
```

## Code Conventions

- TypeScript strict, no `any`
- Named exports only (except page components)
- Response shape: `{ data, error?, meta? }` always
- Never access `process.env` directly — use `config.ts`
- Soft deletes only — never hard delete
- Phase 2/3 features gated by `config.aemApiEnabled` / `config.socialEnabled`

## Scraper

- Playwright headless Chromium — Capella is JS-rendered, static fetch returns nav only
- One shared browser instance per worker — never launch per page
- `waitUntil: 'networkidle'` on every page.goto(), 30s timeout
- 5 concurrent Playwright pages max (heavier than fetch)
- Sitemap XML fetched with plain node-fetch (static, no JS needed)
- One pass per page: extract assets AND testimonials from fully rendered DOM
- Phase 2: testimonials switch to AEM Query Builder, Playwright retained for asset references
- Never launch real Playwright in tests — mock chromium.launch()

## Do Not

- Process bulk audits synchronously
- Set Query Builder queries without explicit `p.limit`
- Write to AEM or modify assets/testimonials
- Store asset binaries — link only
- Commit `.env`
- Write Prisma queries outside repository files
- Render `null` for loading — use skeletons
- Auto-resolve `needs_review` testimonials

## Video Intake — Write Operations

This is the ONLY place the tool writes to AEM. All writes go through `aemUploadService.ts` only.

Intake write account (`AEM_INTAKE_WRITE_USER`) is separate from read-only audit account.

Flow:
1. `POST /api/v1/intake` (public, no auth) → validate → stream video to AEM staging → set metadata → create VideoSubmission → notify approvers → return { submissionId }
2. Approver calls `POST /api/v1/intake/:id/approve` or `POST /api/v1/intake/:id/reject` (internal auth)
3. On full approval → move asset from `/content/dam/capella/intake/pending/` to `/content/dam/capella/{program}/videos/` → update dam:status = approved
4. On rejection → update VideoSubmission.status = rejected → email submitter with reason
5. Submitter resubmits via `POST /api/v1/intake/:id/resubmit` (public) → creates new VideoSubmission with parent_submission_id

AEM write calls:
```
POST /api/assets/capella/intake/pending/{filename}  — upload (stream, never buffer)
PUT  /api/assets/capella/intake/pending/{filename}/jcr:content/metadata  — set tags
MOVE /content/dam/capella/intake/pending/{filename}  — move on approval
PUT  /api/assets/capella/{program}/videos/{filename}/jcr:content/metadata  — update status
```

Approval chain mode from env: `APPROVAL_CHAIN_MODE=sequential | parallel`
- sequential: legal → marketing → publish
- parallel: both notified immediately, both must approve → publish

Status transitions:
```
submitted → pending_review → legal_approved → marketing_approved → approved
                          ↘ rejected (any approver) → notify submitter → resubmitted
```

Public routes: `/intake`, `/intake/confirm`, `/intake/resubmit/:id` — rate limit aggressively
Internal routes: `/admin/intake/*` — require internalAuth middleware

Video files stream directly to AEM — never buffer in memory or write to disk.
AEM staging folder `/content/dam/capella/intake/` must be blocked at dispatcher level (IT config).

## Do Not (updated)
- Write to AEM except through aemUploadService.ts in the intake flow
- Buffer video files in memory — stream directly to AEM
- Expose AEM paths or internal IDs on public-facing intake pages
- Auto-publish AEM pages after approval — asset moves to live DAM only, content authors place it
